#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""skill-surface: Mike's three-layer Aside skill surface.

Layer 1, visible in the Aside menu: the metas in META_INFO plus the rig-skill-surface
router (36 entries as of 2026-10-02; the count is manifest-driven, verify() compares
against m["metas"], not a literal).   ~/.aside/u/0/skills/user/<meta>/SKILL.md
Layer 2 skills and layer 3 sub-skills (hidden):      ~/.aside/u/0/skill-library/<name>/SKILL.md
Data: skill-library/_manifest.json.  Generated by `build`: _nav/<name>.md (one card per skill),
_layers/<meta>.md, INDEX.md, _index.json, TREE.md, <meta>/LAYERS.md, and a marker block in every
real (non-symlink) SKILL.md. Symlinked stores (~/.omp, rig-capabilities) are never written.

Call a skill
  skill-surface where <name> [...]      where it sits, what governs it, what to load (fuzzy ok)
  skill-surface find <words> [--limit N] local ranking by name and purpose
  skill-surface route "<task>" [--local] [--json]
                                        JEV FIRST: meta > skill > sub-skill, one Jev choice per
                                        level with a logged decision id. Secrets are redacted
                                        before hosted JEV. Unredacted private details defer.
                                        --local is retired and uses hosted JEV.
                                        No classifier answering = DEFERRED to local ranking.
  skill-surface tree [meta]
  skill-surface eval [--sensitive]      run the saved routing evals (_route-evals.json); exit 1
                                        if meta accuracy < 0.85
  skill-surface usage [--refresh]       recount real use per skill from chat transcripts
  skill-surface misses [--days N] [--write]   routes that did not land, grouped, for jake-scout
Keep it right
  skill-surface build [--dry-run]       regenerate every map from the manifest
  skill-surface verify                  invariants; exit 1 names every failure
  skill-surface status                  30 visible? strays?
  skill-surface enforce [--apply]       move top-level strays into the library; a reinstall of a
                                        library skill replaces the library copy (old copy parked)
  skill-surface file <name> --meta M [--parent P|none] [--apply]   re-home one skill
  skill-surface restore [--apply]       undo: blocks out, skills back to skills/user, files restored
  skill-surface export [path]           portable tree JSON for the canonical repo (no machine paths)
  skill-surface harness <claude|codex|agents|omp> [--apply] [--restore]
                                        same 30-meta menu in another harness via its native switch
                                        (Claude skillOverrides user-invocable-only; Codex agents/openai.yaml
                                        allow_implicit_invocation false); nothing moves; --restore undoes it
"""
import datetime
import difflib
import hashlib
